00:15:06,842 --> 00:15:10,248
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like, I don't know, I have some kind of...

152
00:15:11,290 --> 00:15:31,420
[SPEAKER_05]: Yeah, physical ailment, literally, and my escape is just to take psychedelic mushrooms, to take myself to this completely different dimension, and then I have this magical expectation that I'll be able to keep up that altered state forever, so that I never have to get united with the old things again.

153
00:15:32,380 --> 00:15:35,362
[SPEAKER_05]: So, now, going back to the previous question,

154
00:15:36,795 --> 00:15:43,299
[SPEAKER_05]: If that's not understanding, then, what is the understanding that you develop, such that you don't suffer anymore?

155
00:15:44,739 --> 00:15:50,082
[SPEAKER_05]: Why all the same mundane things are there, because the five aggregates are the mundane?

156
00:15:54,985 --> 00:16:04,230
[SPEAKER_04]: Well, stopping ignoring the fact that, well, that those things are, well, that whatever you perceive,

157
00:16:05,132 --> 00:16:08,533
[SPEAKER_04]: No matter how special, it's still within perception.

158
00:16:09,333 --> 00:16:14,614
[SPEAKER_04]: And no matter what you feel, no matter how pleasant, it's still within feeling.

159
00:16:16,334 --> 00:16:23,996
[SPEAKER_05]: So, how... what would be... what are you trying to achieve by cultivating that understanding, I guess?

160
00:16:29,617 --> 00:16:33,818
[SPEAKER_04]: Well, not resisting the things the way they are.

161
00:16:33,958 --> 00:16:34,338
[SPEAKER_04]: Exactly.

162
00:16:34,478 --> 00:16:34,698
[SPEAKER_05]: Yeah.

163
00:16:35,432 --> 00:16:40,036
[SPEAKER_05]: So, there's no more magical piece of the puzzle that's missing.

164
00:16:40,857 --> 00:16:44,440
[SPEAKER_05]: Anything more hidden than the fact that when pain is there, you resist it.

165
00:16:45,280 --> 00:16:48,903
[SPEAKER_05]: When pleasure is there, you cannot help yourself but to want more of it.

166
00:16:49,904 --> 00:17:02,895
[SPEAKER_05]: And that's the entire saṃsāra, from the most, kind of, banal, everyday things, to the most subtle, kind of, fetters of immaterial

